BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:epic-megagrants-cycle-2-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T081528Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260904
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260905
SUMMARY:Deadline: Epic MegaGrants 2026 (Cycle 2)
DESCRIPTION:Epic MegaGrants are financial grants from Epic Games for creati
 ve\, noteworthy and innovative projects built in and around Unreal Engine\
 , or projects that enhance the open source 3D graphics ecosystem. Over 2\,
 000 grants have been awarded to date. The programme is explicitly aimed at
  smaller teams\, solo developers and individuals as well as studios: Epic 
 states that individuals and small teams are eligible and encouraged\, and 
 that it treats every project equally regardless of who you are. WHAT IS FU
 NDED: (1) INDIE GAMES\, small or solo teams working in Unreal Engine\, sub
 mitted past the idea and design phase with at least some working prototype
 \, ideally with a video link\; (2) UEFN EXPERIENCES\, Fortnite Creative is
 lands and interactive experiences built in Unreal Editor for Fortnite\; (3
 ) ENGINE MIGRATION\, a proportion of MegaGrants is reserved for teams movi
 ng a partially developed project from another engine to Unreal\; (4) FILM\
 , TV AND LIVE EVENTS\, including live-action and animated films and shows\
 , broadcast\, live and location-based events\; (5) OTHER NON-GAMES VERTICA
 LS such as architecture\, automotive\, manufacturing\, simulation\, produc
 t design\, advertising and VR/AR\, where more detailed project plans and p
 rototypes are expected\; (6) EDUCATION\, including research\, curricula an
 d course development and university programmes\, though for institutions E
 pic accepts submissions only from degree-granting schools and educators at
  such schools\; (7) TOOLS AND OPEN SOURCE\, creating open source tools or 
 enhancing open source software using Unreal Engine. NON-UNREAL PROJECTS AR
 E ELIGIBLE if you want to move them to Unreal Engine\, or if the project e
 nhances open source 3D content creation whether or not it relates to Unrea
 l Engine. EVALUATION rests on three things: quality and unique appeal (hig
 h-quality demos or builds\, well-documented descriptions\, technical ambit
 ion)\; community benefit (how you will give back\, for example open-sourci
 ng the project\, releasing assets through a marketplace\, sharing learning
 s\, or shipping an SDK\, tool or plug-in)\; and viability (a clear budget 
 with major spend areas and a project plan with milestones\, deliverables a
 nd timeline). NOTE ON DEADLINES: the FAQ still describes MegaGrants as an 
 ongoing programme with no specific deadline\, but the timeline published o
 n the same page now runs in fixed cycles\, and the Cycle 2 submission wind
 ow closes 4 September 2026 at 23:59 ET. Treat the cycle date as the operat
 ive deadline. You may apply for more than one project\, and may reapply fo
 r the same project after a decision if you have made updates. Epic is not 
 offering sponsorships and cannot give feedback on applications. Apply at m
 egagrants.unrealengine.com.\n\nOrganisation: Epic Games\nLocation: Open wo
 rldwide. Epic states that if it can legally make payment to you\, you are 
 eligible.\nAward: Typical grants range from USD 5\,000 to USD 75\,000\, wi
 th some exceptional projects receiving up to USD 150\,000. Epic states tha
 t recipients continue to own their IP and may publish it however they wish
 \, so this is a grant rather than an investment or equity deal. Grants up 
 to and including USD 25\,000 may be paid in a single instalment\; larger g
 rants are paid across several instalments tied to continued progress. Fund
 s are for project and team expenses such as development and hiring\; hardw
 are purchases or rentals are approved only occasionally\, case by case. No
  application fee.\nDuration: Cycle 2 of 2026 runs 29 June to 11 December 2
 026. Submission window 29 June to 4 September 2026 (closes 23:59 ET)\, rev
 iew 5 September to 4 December 2026\, notices 7 to 11 December 2026. Cycle 
 1 ran 12 January to 19 June 2026.\n\nMore: https://www.unrealengine.com/me
 gagrants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.unrealengine.com/megagrants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Open worldwide. Epic states that if it can legally make payment to
  you\, you are eligible.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:futures-of-listening-worlding-narratives-roaming-sound-space-2027@artif
 icialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T081528Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260914
SUMMARY:Deadline: Futures of Listening: Worlding Narratives\, Roaming Sound
  Space Residency
DESCRIPTION:One residency to research and develop an interactive listening 
 experience built on non-linear sound narratives\, experienced by navigatin
 g through a series of virtual spaces or layers. NO VISUALS: Worlding Narra
 tives centres sound as the primary medium for immersion and intentionally 
 removes dominant visual layers such as VR\, AR\, projection or video. THE 
 DESIGN PROBLEM they want tackled is translation and adaptation\, specifica
 lly the shift from one visitor in a headphone-mediated experience to rende
 ring for a multi-speaker system for group interaction. That change in dyna
 mics\, reproduction and perspective is integral to the residency scope. RE
 SEARCH QUESTIONS include how immersive sound can function as a primary nar
 rative medium across speculative and non-fictional realities\, what new na
 rrative structures and dramaturgical methods become possible when the crea
 tive process originates from sound rather than adapting frameworks from ot
 her media\, and how interactive sonic structures can create navigable list
 ening experiences designed for and by multiple intelligences. Outcomes may
  include interactive sonic prototypes\, spatial audio compositions\, immer
 sive listening experiences\, narrative sound works or software prototypes.
  WORTH NOTING: your residency runs in tandem with resident Pinar Temiz\, a
 n expert in sound design for gaming environments\, with the opportunity to
  work together. Lead researcher is Dr Angela McArthur of UCL\, with resear
 ch support from Dr meLe yamomo of the University of Amsterdam. WHO: media 
 and sound artists\, sound designers\, musicians producing their own sonic 
 work\, field recordists\, writers\, composers and game sound designers. Ex
 perience with interactive audio\, spatial sound tools or game-sound workfl
 ows is welcome but not required. HARD ELIGIBILITY GATE: applicants must be
  based in the Netherlands AND registered as an artist with the Dutch Chamb
 er of Commerce (KvK). This is not negotiable and rules out non-NL applican
 ts. Futures of Listening is a Netherlands-based platform for spatial sound
 \, immersive experience\, performance and installation art\, founded by FI
 BER Festival\, 4DSOUND\, Robin Koek and Art of Sound at the Royal Conserva
 toire The Hague\, supported by CIIIC and Stimuleringsfonds.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: Futures of Listening (FIBER\, 4DSOUND\, Robin Koek\, Art of Sound)\nLoc
 ation: Amsterdam\, Netherlands\, with remote and studio access to the 4DSO
 UND infrastructure.\nAward: Total residency fee of EUR 7\,125\, calculated
  as 25 commissioned days at a day rate of EUR 285. Six of those 25 days ca
 n be spent at the 4DSOUND studio working with their team. Some additional 
 financial support is available if needed\, including material and travel c
 osts\, but these must be clearly defined and agreed before the residency s
 tarts. No application fee.\nDuration: January to March 2027\, structured a
 s 25 commissioned days\, running in tandem with fellow Worlding Narratives
  resident Pinar Temiz. Deadline 13 September 2026.\n\nMore: https://fiber.
 homerun.co/artist-residency-worlding-narratives/en?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fiber.homerun.co/artist-residency-worlding-narratives/en?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Amsterdam\, Netherlands\, with remote and studio access to the 4DS
 OUND infrastructure.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:screen-australia-future-leaders-bitsummit-2027@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20261030T081528Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261105
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261106
SUMMARY:Deadline: Screen Australia Future Leaders Delegation: BitSummit 202
 7 (Kyoto)
DESCRIPTION:Screen Australia's Future Leaders Delegation sends up to eight 
 early-to-mid career Australian gamemakers to BitSummit 2027 in Kyoto\, Jap
 an (21-23 May 2027)\, one of Asia's leading independent games festivals. S
 UPPORT: AUD 6\,000 per delegate towards flights\, accommodation\, event ti
 ckets\, ground transportation and meals\; travel costs for a mandatory pre
 -departure workshop in Melbourne (mid-April 2027) are covered separately\;
  delegates can exhibit their game as part of an Australia stand. ELIGIBILI
 TY: Australian citizens or permanent residents (individuals) or incorporat
 ed Australian companies with an active ABN and GST registration\; must hav
 e released and/or published at least one game on a public platform\; must 
 be actively developing a game ready for public presentation by May 2027\; 
 must be available for both the workshop and event dates\; must not have pr
 eviously participated in a Screen Australia Future Leaders Delegation. Ass
 essment weighs project quality\, career relevance\, anticipated impact\, a
 nd commitment to diversity and inclusion. HOW TO APPLY: via Screen Austral
 ia's funding portal. Decisions announced by 11 December 2026. DEADLINE: 5 
 November 2026 at 5pm AEST.\n\nOrganisation: Screen Australia\nLocation: De
 legation to BitSummit 2027 in Kyoto\, Japan (21-23 May 2027)\, with a pre-
 departure workshop in Melbourne. Open to Australian citizens or permanent 
 residents\, or incorporated Australian companies.\nAward: AUD 6\,000 per d
 elegate towards flights\, accommodation\, event tickets\, ground transport
 ation and meals\, plus covered travel costs for the pre-departure workshop
  and the opportunity to exhibit a game on the Australia stand. Up to eight
  delegates.\nDuration: BitSummit runs 21-23 May 2027 in Kyoto\; mandatory 
 pre-departure workshop in Melbourne in mid-April 2027\n\nMore: https://www
 .screenaustralia.gov.au/fund/future-leaders-delegation-bitsummit-2027/?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.screenaustralia.gov.au/fund/future-leaders-delegation-bitsu
 mmit-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Delegation to BitSummit 2027 in Kyoto\, Japan (21-23 May 2027)\, w
 ith a pre-departure workshop in Melbourne. Open to Australian citizens or 
 permanent residents\, or incorporated Australian companies.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:processing-foundation-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T081528Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Processing Foundation Fellowship 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Processing Foundation's 2027 fellowship cycle supports arti
 sts\, educators and creative technologists working on open-source projects
 \, with a USD 10\,000 stipend over an 8-month fellowship period. THREE TRA
 CKS: Collective Intelligence (remote\, US-based)\, co-designing AI educati
 on tools with youth\, aimed at educators with software development or AI/M
 L experience\; Gaming the System (hybrid\, Los Angeles)\, building an open
 -source toolkit for video game design with underserved communities\, for g
 ame makers and creative coders based in LA\; and DIY Computing (hybrid\, N
 ew York City)\, developing open-source hardware and software environments 
 for custom computers\, for early-career hardware artists in NYC (applicant
 s currently enrolled in degree programs are ineligible for this track). EL
 IGIBILITY: US applicants only\; hybrid tracks require residency in LA or N
 YC respectively. International applicants are pointed to the Foundation's 
 Microgrants and Processing Community Day instead. APPLICATION: via nominat
 ion form\, selecting one track\; self-nominations are allowed. Selection b
 y a panel of the Processing Foundation team and external reviewers\, judgi
 ng strength of the project\, fit with the Foundation's mission and potenti
 al impact. TIMELINE: nominations open 7 October 2026\, close 1 November 20
 26 at 11:59 PM PST\; fellows notified 14 December 2026\; fellowship runs 2
 5 January to 26 September 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Processing Foundation\nLo
 cation: USA only. The Collective Intelligence track is remote (US-based)\;
  Gaming the System is hybrid in Los Angeles\; DIY Computing is hybrid in N
 ew York City.\nAward: USD 10\,000 stipend over the 8-month fellowship\, pl
 us open-source software mentorship\, cohort collaboration\, professional d
 evelopment and public presentation opportunities. No application fee.\nDur
 ation: Approximately 8 months\, 25 January to 26 September 2027.\n\nMore: 
 https://processingfoundation.org/programs/fellowships/fellowship-2027/?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://processingfoundation.org/programs/fellowships/fellowship-2027/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:USA only. The Collective Intelligence track is remote (US-based)\;
  Gaming the System is hybrid in Los Angeles\; DIY Computing is hybrid in N
 ew York City.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:creative-europe-media-video-games-immersive-content-2027@artificialnouv
 eau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T081528Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270202
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270203
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative Europe MEDIA: European Video Games and Immersive
  Content Development 2027 (up to EUR 200\,000)
DESCRIPTION:The MEDIA strand's annual development scheme for video games an
 d immersive content (call CREA-MEDIA-2027-DEVVGIM) funds the pre-productio
 n of interactive narrative works with original content and quality gamepla
 y intended for commercial release on PC\, console\, mobile or XR platforms
 . WHAT IT FUNDS: concept and prototype development up to a first playable\
 , vertical slice\, alpha or demo\; production-phase work is excluded\, as 
 are puzzle\, sports\, racing\, quiz and party genres. WHO: European video 
 game production companies\, XR studios and audiovisual production companie
 s whose main activity is game or software development or audiovisual produ
 ction\, established in a country fully participating in MEDIA and majority
 -owned by nationals of such countries. Publishers and natural persons cann
 ot apply. The coordinator must have produced or developed a game or immers
 ive experience commercially distributed between 1 January 2024 and the dea
 dline\, evidenced by a sales report (work-for-hire and Early Access titles
  do not count)\, and must hold the majority of rights. WHAT YOU GET: a lum
 p sum of up to EUR 200\,000 (60 percent of the estimated budget) from a EU
 R 13.5 million pot. APPLICATION: single stage via the EU Funding and Tende
 rs Portal. DEADLINE: 2 February 2027 at 17:00 Brussels time.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Creative Europe MEDIA (European Commission / EACEA)\nLocation: EU Memb
 er States\, EEA and countries associated to Creative Europe MEDIA. For gam
 e and XR production companies established and majority-owned in a MEDIA co
 untry.\nAward: Lump-sum grant of up to EUR 200\,000 per project\, set at 6
 0 percent of the estimated budget. Total call budget EUR 13\,500\,000. No 
 application fee.\nDuration: Development from concept to first playable pro
 totype (first playable\, vertical slice\, alpha\, demo). Call opened 30 Se
 ptember 2026.\n\nMore: https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportuni
 ties/portal/screen/opportunities/topic-details/CREA-MEDIA-2027-DEVVGIM?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/o
 pportunities/topic-details/CREA-MEDIA-2027-DEVVGIM?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:EU Member States\, EEA and countries associated to Creative Europe
  MEDIA. For game and XR production companies established and majority-owne
 d in a MEDIA country.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:screen-australia-emerging-gamemakers-fund-2027@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20261030T081528Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270225
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270226
SUMMARY:Deadline: Screen Australia: Emerging Gamemakers Fund (round closing
